  "problem": "Expressed as a decimal in its simplest form, $(-1.6)^{3}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "To work out $(-1.6)^{3},$ we multiply $-1.6$ by itself and then multiply the result by $-1.6$ once more:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1.6)^{3} & =\\overset{2.56}{\\overset{⏞}{(-1.6)\\cdot (-1.6)}}\\cdot (-1.6) \\\\  & =2.56\\cdot (-1.6) \\\\  & =-4.096\\end{aligned}\n$$",
